  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U12L-READ-1",
      "title": "The Old Temple Trip",
      "text": "Our history teacher took us to an old temple in the central area of Tainan. The temple is more than two hundred years old, and many people go there to worship every month. Inside, we saw Chinese characters carved on a big wooden board. Our teacher said the work took three years. She gave us a clue and asked us to find the name of the god on the wall; the first hint was the color red. She also asked, \"Are you with me?\" before every long explanation. Then Ken wanted to shake the fortune sticks, but the temple was closing. On the way home, our school vehicle broke down. It was nobody's fault; the bus was simply old. We could not figure out why it stopped, so we waited an hour."
    }
  ],
